
Scalable R&D and "Outside-the-Box" Innovation

Internal corporate teams are often burdened by daily operational tasks, leaving little room for experimental research.
• Fresh Perspectives: Gen-Z college students bring cutting-edge academic knowledge, familiarity with the latest open-source tools, and uninhibited creative thinking to complex business problems.
• Low-Risk R&D: Companies can crowdsource proof-of-concepts (PoCs) or prototype multiple solutions for a single problem simultaneously across different colleges, without exhausting internal engineering hours.